## Rationale
Adjusted from high to ignore for security triage. The code and validation evidence show a real product liveness bug, but not a high-severity security vulnerability. The affected path is an internal control-plane/storage-node heartbeat mechanism over private Unix sockets, and the required trigger is operational downtime, clock movement, or no committed heartbeats for more than one hour. No repository evidence connects unauthenticated or authenticated S3 HTTP clients to control of authority_now_ms, process restarts, persisted max_committed_timestamp_ms, or storage-node heartbeat contents. The impact can be severe operational availability loss, but without a realistic in-scope attacker-controlled entry point it would not meet high/critical security acceptance criteria.
## Likelihood
low - The bug is plausibly triggered by ordinary downtime, restart after inactivity, or clock jumps, but repository evidence does not show a realistic external attacker can cause the stale timestamp/restart condition or access the private control-plane socket.
## Impact
medium - If the operational preconditions occur, the distributed storage service can suffer total availability loss until manual repair. The effect is availability-only, with no demonstrated confidentiality, integrity, identity, or code-execution impact.
## Assumptions
- Assessment is based only on repository artifacts and the provided validation evidence; no cloud APIs or live deployment were queried.
- No Kubernetes, Terraform, Docker Compose, or other deployment manifests were found/used to prove public exposure of the control-plane path.
- Storage-node/control-plane Unix socket access is treated as internal/trusted unless an attacker already has local filesystem access to the private socket directory.
- existing persisted control-plane state with max_committed_timestamp_ms set
- control plane has no committed timestamp progress for more than MAX_COMMITTED_TIMESTAMP_FORWARD_JUMP_MS, currently 1 hour
- restart, long downtime, long inactivity in distributed control-plane mode, or a large local clock jump
- storage nodes then need to renew heartbeat leases
